Revert 0138: restore the original ATM commpage behaviour (fixes logd).

0138 masked ATM_TRACE_DISABLE out of the commpage view of atm_diagnostic_config
while keeping it internally.  Measured consequence with 0139 in the same
kernel: userspace sees atm_diagnostic_config == 0, libsystem_trace/os_trace
re-enables tracing while the kernel firehose is disabled, and logd
SIGTRAP crash-loops ("CRASH logd sig 5 code 0x600000001"); the GUIX10K cycle
never reached "SWEET FB: display on".

The SpringBoard PaperBoardUI nil-block crash that 0138 worked around is fixed
on the userspace side (dyld shared cache NOP of BaseBoard's `cbz x0` at unslid
0x18dd5b934, in tmp/iosroot28.simg), so 0138 is not needed.

0140 is the exact inverse of 0138 on current main (0139 touched only
bsd/dev/sweet_sample.c):
  - osfmk/atm/atm.c: atm_get_diagnostic_config() returns the raw
    atm_diagnostic_config again; the 0138 sweet_oslog_off boot arg / banner and
    atm_get_kernel_diagnostic_config() are removed;
  - osfmk/atm/atm_internal.h: the extra accessor declaration is removed;
  - libkern/os/log.c: oslog_init() restores
    `oslog_disabled = atm_get_diagnostic_config() & ATM_TRACE_DISABLE;`.

After this the kernel is mathematically back to the pre-0138 ATM code (byte
identical to the original CI files), so userspace sees the boot-arg
`atm_diagnostic_config=256` bit again, tracing stays disabled everywhere and
logd is healthy; 0139's KLOG fixes are untouched.
